{
  "status": "inconclusive",
  "findings": [
    "Direct support for the exact claim and its stated scope: The claim asserts five symbol-to-name mappings. Three are directly supported at the token level by the supplied citations. KEGG COMPOUND C00270 lists 'Neu5Ac' in the same NAME block as 'N-Acetylneuraminic acid', and a second quote from the same record renders the entry as 'C00270  N-Acetylneuraminic acid', supporting Neu5Ac = N-acetylneuraminic acid. KEGG C00140 lists 'GlcNAc' in the same NAME block as 'N-Acetyl-D-glucosamine', supporting GlcNAc = N-acetylglucosamine (the claim omits the D- locant, which is a narrowing of specificity rather than a conflict). The ChEBI CHEBI:28037 synonym list contains both 'GalNAc' and 'N-Acetyl-D-galactosamine', with KEGG C01132 naming the same compound 'N-Acetyl-D-galactosamine', supporting GalNAc = N-acetylgalactosamine. Two of the five mappings are not supported by any supplied quote: no citation contains the token 'Man' or the word 'mannose', and no citation contains the token 'Fuc'. The only fucose-related quote gives '6-Deoxy-L-galactose' and '6-deoxy-L-galactopyranose', which are alternative systematic names and do not establish the abbreviation Fuc or pair it with the name 'fucose' in the supplied text. The parenthetical gloss '(sialic acid)' attached to Neu5Ac likewise appears in no supplied quote. Because the claim is a conjunction of five mappings plus one parenthetical, and 40 percent of the mappings plus the parenthetical are unsupported, the exact claim as stated is not fully evidenced within its scope.",
    "Source applicability, qualifications and conflicting evidence: The source types are appropriate in kind but only partially applicable to the stated scope. The claim's scope is explicitly 'IUPAC condensed / standard glycan monosaccharide symbol-to-name mapping as used in glycan notation'. KEGG COMPOUND and the EMBL-EBI Ontology Lookup Service record for ChEBI are chemical compound and ontology resources; they happen to carry several of the glycan-notation abbreviations as synonyms, which is why the Neu5Ac, GlcNAc and GalNAc mappings can be read off them, but they are not authorities on glycan condensed notation and they do not systematically enumerate that notation's symbol set. This explains the observed gaps rather than resolving them: the absence of 'Man' and 'Fuc' from these records is a limit of source applicability, not evidence against the mappings. Qualification notes: the KEGG Neu5Ac evidence spans a NAME block and a BRITE-style line from the same record (reference_ref 5cfeed44...), so those two quotes are not independent sources; the GalNAc mapping rests on one ChEBI synonym list for the abbreviation plus one KEGG line for the name. No supplied citation contradicts any part of the claim. In particular, nothing in the quotes asserts a different expansion for Neu5Ac, GlcNAc, GalNAc, Man or Fuc, so the packet contains unsupported elements but no conflicting evidence, which rules out a fail under the status rules.",
    "Uncertainty and limits of a documentary conclusion: This assessment is documentary only, consistent with the rubric boundary. It compares the claim text against the supplied quotes and asserts nothing about tested behavior or scientific performance. The packet's own limitations statement confirms that the subject skill was never executed for this claim, so the claim's expected_behavior ('the skill returns the corresponding full monosaccharide name as tabulated') is entirely unverified here: even for the three mappings whose nomenclature is corroborated, no evidence shows that the skill emits them. The packet further records that the required grade-critique step failed three times in this run and that one retrieved reference (Essentials of Glycobiology chapter 1, NBK579927) could not be displayed and is therefore unquoted; that unquoted reference is plausibly the source that would cover Man, Fuc and the sialic-acid class label, but an undisplayed reference cannot support a finding. The residual uncertainty is therefore asymmetric: the unsupported mappings are widely used conventions that a suitable glycan-notation reference would likely corroborate, but under this rubric only supplied citations count. Support is insufficient to certify every criterion within the exact scope, and no citation contradicts the claim, so the correct disposition is inconclusive rather than pass or fail."
  ],
  "citations": [
    {
      "reference_ref": "5cfeed44d6503ab54a60fa31bc8e9a279567e4a341260dcc95f5aa0a8debe99e",
      "quote": "NAME        N-Acetylneuraminate;\n            N-Acetylneuraminic acid;\n            5-Acetamido-3,5-dideoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-2-nonulosonic acid;\n            Neu5Ac"
    },
    {
      "reference_ref": "5cfeed44d6503ab54a60fa31bc8e9a279567e4a341260dcc95f5aa0a8debe99e",
      "quote": "C00270  N-Acetylneuraminic acid"
    },
    {
      "reference_ref": "f4376c514837bf653af186707ee000343bfd55c10d07f330a9cc4d18b4966e00",
      "quote": "NAME        N-Acetyl-D-glucosamine;\n            N-Acetylchitosamine;\n            2-Acetamido-2-deoxy-D-glucose;\n            GlcNAc"
    },
    {
      "reference_ref": "fa81c3e4d77781be6dbd17ae0a2f8df4d421f38120de0892e8b3885116a80388",
      "quote": "\"synonyms\" : [ \"2-Acetamido-2-deoxy-D-galactose\", \"2-acetamido-2-deoxy-D-galactopyranose\", \"2-acetamido-2-deoxy-D-galactopyranose\", \"D-GalNAc\", \"GalNAc\", \"N-Acetyl-D-chondrosamine\", \"N-Acetyl-D-galactosamine\", \"N-acetyl-D-galactosamine\" ]"
    },
    {
      "reference_ref": "5128fa08da033a50109bb6a90f0976e10159f47afbce419bbbfdc9df138835b5",
      "quote": "C01132  N-Acetyl-D-galactosamine"
    },
    {
      "reference_ref": "ee9247fa0409874abebd4f5944ea77562776d445763e869e14bd7ee920859f03",
      "quote": "\"6-Deoxy-L-galactose\", \"6-deoxy-L-galactopyranose\""
    }
  ],
  "limitations": "Scope of this assessment: documentary consistency between the claim text and the six supplied quotes only, under rubric local-documentary-v1. No tool use, no retrieval beyond the packet, and no assertion of tested scientific performance. Specific limits: (1) Two of the claim's five mappings, Man = mannose and Fuc = fucose, have no supporting token in any supplied quote; the fucose quote supplies only systematic synonyms. (2) The parenthetical '(sialic acid)' for Neu5Ac is unsupported by the supplied quotes, and the packet notes KEGG places Neu5Ac under amino sugars rather than a sialic-acid label; that classification text was not itself supplied as a quote, so this assessor treats the gloss as unsupported rather than contradicted. (3) The two Neu5Ac quotes share one reference_ref and are not independent corroboration. (4) The claim's expected_behavior concerns skill output; the packet states no execution occurred, so nothing here speaks to what the skill actually returns. (5) One retrieved reference (NCBI Bookshelf NBK579927) was pinned but undisplayed and contributed no quotes, so any coverage it might provide for the unsupported mappings could not be assessed. (6) Absence of evidence in this packet is not treated as evidence of error; the status reflects insufficient support, not detected falsity."
}

